# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-13, R-4, RC-6). L §5.14.2 Takes in the first batch: "A cycle among them (two places
# sweeping into each other in one batch, each arrival keeping labels) breaks where it can: each take is tried with the
# cycle's arrivals as parts of unknown labels, and a take whose outcome is the same under every reading of them ... is
# decided, which breaks the cycle. Otherwise a cycle that holds a plan is refused (RUN-CYCLE, naming the movements) ...
# A cycle of observed rows only is an unknown fact ...: the takes it reaches are undecided, each place holds a hole part
# with its total known (§8.1)".
# L §5.14 "A movement's take never includes its own arrivals": one movement sw moves 30.00 from konto to konto2 (leg x)
# and 20.00 back (leg y). Each place's group reads the other's take, but tried with the other's arrival as a part of
# unknown labels, sw.x's take skips its own arrival y and sw.y's skips x: both are decided, the cycle breaks, and the
# labels are known (scratch/exp6.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind lots: place PLN min 0
  batched
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order k.batch.day
kind swaps: event certain
  leg x: PLN
  leg y: PLN
place konto: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place konto2: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input b1_day: date
input b1_amt: money PLN
input b2_day: date
input b2_amt: money PLN
input sw_x: money PLN
input sw_day: date
input sw_y: money PLN
move sw: swaps
  on sw_day
  leg x from konto to konto2 amount sw_x
  leg y from konto2 to konto amount sw_y
move b1: transfers
  on b1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount b1_amt
move b2: transfers
  on b2_day
  leg cash from world to konto2 amount b2_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-01), bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of b1, bal(konto2, 2026-03-01), bal(konto2, 2026-03-01) of b2, sw.x.amount of b1, sw.y.amount of b2, bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of b2, bal(konto2, 2026-03-01) of b1

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto2] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  b1_day = 2026-02-01
  b1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  b2_day = 2026-02-15
  b2_amt = 50.00 PLN
  sw_day = 2026-03-01
  sw_x = 30.00 PLN
  sw_y = 20.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (90.00 PLN, 70.00 PLN, 60.00 PLN, 30.00 PLN, 30.00 PLN, 20.00 PLN, 20.00 PLN, 30.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
